# Smoke run artefacts (screenshots, traces, HTML reports) are written here
# by tests/smoke/run.sh under <run-date>/ subdirectories. They are useful
# locally for human review but should not be committed — each run is
# unique and the binaries (PNGs, .zip traces, video) bloat the repo.
#
# The directory itself is checked in (with this .gitignore + README) so
# the smoke runner does not need to mkdir it on first run.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
